 Buddhism with Chiara Mascarello\, PhD
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T073000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T081500
DTSTAMP:20261020T174746Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53048023123167-53048032875781@local-events
DESCRIPTION:This session offers a gentle introduction to a contemplative p
 ractice inspired by Tibetan Buddhist traditions\, exploring the movement o
 f the mind and its deeper qualities. Beginning with the breath as a suppor
 t for settling and stabilising attention\, participants will be invited to
  observe thoughts as they arise and pass\, and to gradually rest in a more
  open\, spacious quality of presence. \n\nChiara Mascarello\, PhD\, has pu
 rsued research in Buddhist philosophy and Tibetan language at Sera Jey Mon
 as\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://med.stanford.edu/contemplation/summi
 t.html\nLast synced: 2026-10-20 10:47 PDT
