DTSTAMP:20261020T174746Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54127017917925-54127017918950@local-events
DESCRIPTION:In the 1970s and 1980s\, dissident artists associated with Sou
 th Korea's minjung (people's) art movement rejected both state-sponsored m
 odernism and imported Cold War formalism. Yet their opposition to authorit
 arian rule did not entail a rejection of tradition. Instead\, they turned 
 to precolonial vernacular practices—Buddhist visual traditions\, folk im
 agery\, communal performance\, and indigenous cultural practices—as crit
 ical resources for political expression. Drawing on The Minjung Art Moveme
 nt:\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-20 10:47 PDT
LOCATION:Lathrop Library
END:VEVENT
